[statement]
A candidate whose dependency nothing can answer is passed over where
another candidate for the name depends on the package that requires it:
`b` needs `a`; `a` 3, the best candidate, needs `missing`, which nothing
provides, and `a` 1 needs `b`; apk installs `a` 1. Without the dependency
of `a` 1 on `b`, apk refuses
(`a-candidate-whose-dependency-cannot-be-met-is-not-passed-over-below-a-package`).

[repository]
P:a
V:1
D:b

P:a
V:3
D:missing

P:b
V:2
D:a

[request]
b

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install a 1
install b 2
